                <pb facs="0487" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg379"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Durham to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 178.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge receipt of dispatch
                    No. 101, of February 16, relative to the case of Mr. Mevs.</p>
                <p>Notwithstanding my acceptance of President Hyppolite’s offer under instructions
                    from the Department, I have not yet succeeded in making any formal
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John S. Durham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
